# Windows totally on virtual disk [TO TEST]


## DISM : Create image *.wim
`dism /capture-image /imagefile:"D:\Win10Backup.wim" /capturedir:c:\ /name:"Win10Backup"`


## Prepare virtual disk : 
```cmd
(as admin) > diskpart
create vdisk file="D:\Win10Pro.vhdx" maximum=81920
select vdisk file="D:\Win10Pro.vhdx"
attach vdisk
create partition primary
format quick fs=ntfs label="VHDX"
assign letter=V
```

## DISM : Restore image *.wim

`dism /Get-ImageInfo /ImageFile:"D:\Win10Backup.wim"`
or  
`dism /get-wiminfo /wimfile:"D:\Win10Backup.wim"`

`dism /apply-image /imagefile:"D:\Win10Backup.wim" /index:6 /applydir:V:\ `


## Add Boot Entry
bcdboot V:\Windows

